HTML5 (1–8)

1. section = thematic grouping, article = self-contained content, div = no semantic meaning.


2. <main> represents primary content; must be unique for accessibility and SEO.


3. Semantic HTML improves accessibility, SEO, maintainability.


4. data-* stores custom data without affecting semantics; better than classes for JS hooks.


5. localStorage = persistent, sessionStorage = tab-based, cookies = sent with requests.


6. <picture> allows different images per screen size/device.


7. Groups media with caption for semantic meaning.


8. Uses input types, required, pattern, min/max.




